@mtworth One thing that helped us a lot: stripping page noise before it ever reaches the model. Cookie banners, footers, chat widgets, recommended content. None of it is relevant to the task but it all burns context. 

We actually built a browser extension specifically for this called Agent Browser Shield. It sits between browser-use and the web and cleans the page before the agent sees it (mostly meant to help with security and prevent prompt injection, but strips out unnnecessary garbage on the page to reduce context).

Free and open source: https://github.com/pixiebrix/agent-browser-shield

